-- title:
--   Localisation of the base commutes with chart algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $K$ a commutative $R$-algebra and $F$ a field that is both an $R$-algebra and a $K$-algebra, the two structures being compatible in the sense that $R \to K \to F$ is a scalar tower; assume moreover that $K$ is a localisation of $R$ at a submonoid $M \subseteq R$, and let $S$ be an arbitrary subset of $F$ (all three carrier types lying in one universe). For a base ring $B$ acting on $F$, `chartAlg B F S` denotes the $B$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of those elements of $F$ that are integral over the $B$-subalgebra $B[S] =$ `Algebra.adjoin B S` generated by $S$. The assertion is that there exists an isomorphism of $K$-algebras $$e : K \otimes_R \operatorname{chartAlg}(R,F,S) \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \operatorname{chartAlg}(K,F,S)$$ which is compatible with the inclusions into $F$ on pure tensors: for every $q \in K$ and every $b$ in `chartAlg R F S`, the element $e(q \otimes b)$, viewed in $F$, equals $q \cdot b$, the scalar action of $q$ on the image of $b$ in $F$. Thus $e$ is not merely abstract but is the expected multiplication map.
--
--   This is the statement that forming the integral closure commutes with localisation of the base ring, expressed in terms of the chart algebras of the two-chart integral model: taking $S = \{j\}$ and $S = \{j^{-1}\}$ it identifies, chart by chart, the base change to $K$ of the model over $R$ with the model formed directly over $K$. It is used to compare the generic fibre of the two-chart integral model with its pullback to the base, and hence in the smoothness and residue-field computations for these models.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_exists_algEquiv_tensor_chartAlg.lean

